From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:10:00 +0000
Subject: wireless: uwe5622: do not cancel the loopcheck work from itself

When the firmware misses a loopcheck ack, loopcheck_work_queue() calls
stop_loopcheck() and then mdbg_assert_interface(), whose CP2 reset
calls stop_loopcheck() again through marlin_set_power(). Both run in
the loopcheck work, and stop_loopcheck() does cancel_delayed_work_sync()
on that work: it waits for itself forever. The CP2 reset never
finishes, WLAN and Bluetooth stay dead until reboot, and every later
stop_loopcheck() (e.g. the WLAN command timeout reset) blocks too.

Seen on an Orange Pi Zero2 after an SDIO CMD53 timeout under full
system load (hung task reports for both paths).

Skip the synchronous cancel when stop_loopcheck() runs in the loopcheck
work; that work does not requeue itself once the open bit is clear.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/platform/loopcheck.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/platform/loopcheck.c
@@ -210,7 +210,12 @@
 		return;
 	WCN_INFO("%s\n", __func__);
 	complete_all(&loopcheck.completion);
-	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&loopcheck.work);
+	/*
+	 * The work stops loopcheck itself when an ack is missing, directly
+	 * and through the CP2 reset; it must not wait for its own end.
+	 */
+	if (current_work() != &loopcheck.work.work)
+		cancel_delayed_work_sync(&loopcheck.work);
 }
 
 void complete_kernel_loopcheck(void)
